k compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 3.4x net debt to EBITDA ($700.7M of cash against $10.2B of debt), with interest covered 3.5x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.65 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD.","Goodwill makes up 43% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 5.5% over 3 years, 3.4% over 5 years and -0.1% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 14%).","At current returns, reinvesting 1% of profits supports about 0.1% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 0.1% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.8x, 4.2% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 12, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 10.0% on average."],"own":["Insiders own 47.0%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 50%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (10 sales, net $137.6M sold).","It returns 10.9% a year to shareholders (10.9% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 8.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 15.3% of the float, 7.5 days to cover."],"people":["With about 78,000 employees, each generates about $175K of revenue, 0.5x the Healthcare median, and productivity has risen 4.0% a year.","That works out to $17K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $4.1M (23x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":70,"head":"Invest: trades 76% below fair value of $793; ROIC 16.0% vs WACC 8.0%.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 50, gates 13/25)","Trades 76% below fair value of $793","ROIC 16.0% vs WACC 8.0%","P/E 14.5x vs sector 25.5x","EV/EBITDA 9.4x vs sector 15.7x"],"cons":["Net debt/EBITDA 3.4x","Altman Z in the distress zone (1.65)","Heavy